e insertion/deletion RNA editing in trypanosome mitochondria: a complex business</article-title><source>RNA</source><year>2003</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>265</fpage><lpage>276</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12591999</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B12"><label>12</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Madison-Antenucci</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Grams</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Hajduk</surname><given-names>SL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Editing machines: the complexities of trypanosome RNA editing</article-title><source>Cell</source><year>2002</year><volume>108</volume><fpage>435</fpage><lpage>438</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11909515</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B13"><label>13</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Carpenter</surname><given-names>LR</given-names></name><name><surname>Englund</surname><given-names>PT</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Kinetoplast maxicircle DNA replication in <italic>Crithidia fasciculata</italic> and <italic>Trypanosoma brucei</italic></article-title><source>Mol. Cell. Biol.</source><year>1995</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>6794</fpage><lpage>6803</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8524245</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B14"><label>14</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Englund</surname><given-names>PT</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Free minicircles of kinetoplast DNA networks in <italic>Crithidia fasciculata</italic></article-title><source>J. Biol. Chem.</source><year>1979</year><volume>254</volume><fpage>4895</fpage><lpage>4900</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">438220</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B15"><label>15</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Drew</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surname>Englund</surname><given-names>PT</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Intramitochondrial location and dynamics of <italic>Crithidia fasciculata</italic> kinetoplast minicircle replication intermediates</article-title><source>J. Cell Biol.</source><year>2001</year><volume>153</volume><fpage>735</fpage><lpage>744</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11352935</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B16"><label>16</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Melendy</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Sheline</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Ray</surname><given-names>DS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Localization of a type II DNA topoisomerase to two sites at the periphery of the kinetoplast DNA of <italic>Crithidia fasciculata</italic></article-title><source>Cell</source><year>1988</year><volume>55</volume><fpage>1083</fpage><lpage>1088</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2849507</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B17"><label>17</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><name><surname>Englund</surname><given-names>PT</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>RNA interference of a trypanosome topoisomerase II causes progressive loss of mitochondrial DNA</article-title><source>EMBO J.</source><year>2001</year><volume>20</volume><fpage>4674</fpage><lpage>4683</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11532932</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B18"><label>18</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Perez-Morga</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Englund</surname><given-names>PT</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The structure of replicating kinetoplast DNA networks</article-title><source>J. Cell Biol.</source><year>1993</year><volume>123</volume><fpage>1069</fpage><lpage>1079</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8245118</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B19"><label>19</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Guilbride</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Englund</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The replication mechanism of kinetoplast DNA networks in several trypanosomatid species</article-title><source>J. Cell Sci.</source><year>1998</year><volume>111</volume><fpage>675</fpage><lpage>679</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9471996</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B20"><label>20</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Liu</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Englund</surname><given-names>PT</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The rotational dynamics of kinetoplast DNA replication</article-title><source>Mol. Microbiol.</source><year>2007</year><volume>64</volume><fpage>676</fpage><lpage>690</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17462016</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B21"><label>21</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ray</surname><given-names>DS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Conserved sequence blocks in kinetoplast minicircles from diverse species of trypanosomes</article-title><source>Mol. Cell. Biol.</source><year>1989</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>1365</fpage><lpage>1367</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2542768</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B22"><label>22</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Birkenmeyer</surn